<title>FRANCE: Sanofi shares suspended pending statement.</title>
<headline>Sanofi shares suspended pending statement.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in health and beauty products group Sanofi were suspended at 1230 GMT on Wednesday at the request of the company pending a statement, the French Bourses' Association SBF said.</p>
<p>The share had been rising another 0.75 percent to 470 francs in anticipation of a positive result of a U.S. study on Sanofi's Clopidogrel drug. It also posted gains on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Sanofi will brief journalists in Paris later on Wednesday on the results of the clinical studies which will be officially announced at 2100 GMT in New Orleans at the annual congress of the U.S. Association of Cardiologists.</p>
<p>If the results of the tests are positive, Sanofi intends to start a market registration procedure for the cardio-vascular product to be sold as Plavix.</p>
<p>Sanofi is majority-owned by Elf-Aquitaine.</p>
</text>
